            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53489",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/containerd/containerd: containerd: Arbitrary host file read via symlink following in CRI checkpoint restore"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "containerd is an open-source container runtime. Versions prior to 2.3.2, 2.2.5 and 2.1.9 contain a bug where the CRI plugin restores container.log from a checkpoint image without validating a symlinked path. This could result in reading an arbitrary file on the host via kubectl logs. This issue has been fixed in versions 2.3.2, 2.2.5 and 2.1.9."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53489",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53489\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/containerd/containerd/v2\nFixed Version: 2.1.9, 2.2.5, 2.3.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-53489](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53489)\ncontainerd is an open-source container runtime. Versions prior to 2.3.2, 2.2.5 and 2.1.9 contain a bug where the CRI plugin restores container.log from a checkpoint image without validating a symlinked path. This could result in reading an arbitrary file on the host via kubectl logs. This issue has been fixed in versions 2.3.2, 2.2.5 and 2.1.9.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53489**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/containerd/containerd/v2|2.1.9, 2.2.5, 2.3.2|[CVE-2026-53489](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53489)|\n\ncontainerd is an open-source container runtime. Versions prior to 2.3.2, 2.2.5 and 2.1.9 contain a bug where the CRI plugin restores container.log from a checkpoint image without validating a symlinked path. This could result in reading an arbitrary file on the host via kubectl logs. This issue has been fixed in versions 2.3.2, 2.2.5 and 2.1.9."
              },
              "properties": {
