            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-47262",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/containerd/containerd: containerd: Denial of Service via maliciously crafted image leading to unbounded group parsing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "containerd is an open-source container runtime. Versions prior to 1.7.33, 2.0.10, 2.1.9, 2.2.5 and 2.3.2, contain a vulnerability that allows a maliciously crafted image to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) condition. When creating a container from this image, memory exhaustion occurs, leading to an Out Of Memory (OOM) kill of the containerd process. This renders the container runtime API unavailable and can disrupt clients such as the Docker Engine or Kubernetes control-plane components. This issue has been fixed in versions 1.7.33, 2.0.10, 2.1.9, 2.2.5 and 2.3.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-47262",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-47262\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/containerd/containerd/v2\nFixed Version: 2.0.10, 2.1.9, 2.2.5, 2.3.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-47262](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-47262)\ncontainerd is an open-source container runtime. Versions prior to 1.7.33, 2.0.10, 2.1.9, 2.2.5 and 2.3.2, contain a vulnerability that allows a maliciously crafted image to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) condition. When creating a container from this image, memory exhaustion occurs, leading to an Out Of Memory (OOM) kill of the containerd process. This renders the container runtime API unavailable and can disrupt clients such as the Docker Engine or Kubernetes control-plane components. This issue has been fixed in versions 1.7.33, 2.0.10, 2.1.9, 2.2.5 and 2.3.2.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-47262**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/containerd/containerd/v2|2.0.10, 2.1.9, 2.2.5, 2.3.2|[CVE-2026-47262](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-47262)|\n\ncontainerd is an open-source container runtime. Versions prior to 1.7.33, 2.0.10, 2.1.9, 2.2.5 and 2.3.2, contain a vulnerability that allows a maliciously crafted image to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) condition. When creating a container from this image, memory exhaustion occurs, leading to an Out Of Memory (OOM) kill of the containerd process. This renders the container runtime API unavailable and can disrupt clients such as the Docker Engine or Kubernetes control-plane components. This issue has been fixed in versions 1.7.33, 2.0.10, 2.1.9, 2.2.5 and 2.3.2."
              },
